---
/* CAREFUL — do not turn this into a MAT offer. The client wiki states MAT is on
   hold and must not be referenced as a service, and admissions confirms there
   is no methadone programme here. A meaningful share of fentanyl callers are
   already on methadone or buprenorphine, so the section exists to get that
   raised early and reviewed clinically, not to promise continuation. Admissions
   handles it exactly this way: the doctors review the assessment and decide.
   Keep the wording non-committal on continuation. */
---
<section id="on-medication" class="bg-sage-tint py-[70px]">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <p class="text-gold font-body text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.18em] uppercase mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
      <span class="w-6 h-px bg-gold inline-block"></span>
      If you are already on something
    </p>
    <h2 class="font-display text-charcoal mb-6">
      On methadone or Suboxone? Say so at the start.
    </h2>

    <div class="space-y-5 font-body text-charcoal text-[17px] leading-[29px]">
      <p>
        Arriving already on a maintenance medication is common, and it is not a complication anyone will be annoyed about. What it does mean is that our clinical team needs to know early — the doctors review your assessment and make a plan around it, and that is a far better conversation to have before you arrive than on the day.
      </p>
      <p>
        So when you call, lead with it: what you are on, the dose, and how long you have been taking it. The same goes for anything prescribed for pain, anxiety, sleep or a mental health condition. Bring the bottles if you have them.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong class="font-bold">Being on a prescribed medication does not put treatment out of reach.</strong> It just means the planning starts a step earlier, and getting it right is worth the extra two minutes on the phone.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-white border-l-2 border-gold rounded-r-xl p-6 mt-8">
      <p class="font-body text-charcoal text-[16px] leading-[27px]">
        Not sure whether your situation fits? That is exactly the sort of thing the first call is for. Ring
        <a href="tel:8883625576" class="text-teal font-semibold hover:opacity-70 transition-opacity tel-number">(888) 362-5576</a>
        and describe it as it actually is — the team will tell you plainly what they think, and help you find the right programme either way.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
